From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 21:56:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] usb: mtu3: reconnect after a suspend taken with a suspended
 bus

With a suspended bus allowed to suspend the system, the gadget can go
to sleep still marked connected. The system suspend powers the device
IP and port down, which drops the link and the D+ pullup, and resume
powers them on again without either: the gadget stayed "not attached"
after a replug on the Gemini until a soft disconnect and connect from
userspace re-asserted the pullup.

Treat such a suspend as the disconnect it is: take the pullup down,
report the disconnect to the gadget driver and drop the connection's
runtime PM reference. At resume, assert the pullup again if the gadget
wants it, so the host can enumerate the device afresh.
---
 drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_core.c | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_core.c b/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_core.c
index ecae7a057..a64b0b13e 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_core.c
@@ -1045,6 +1045,26 @@ int ssusb_gadget_suspend(struct ssusb_mtk *ssusb, pm_message_t msg)
 	if (mtu->connected && !mtu->bus_suspended)
 		return -EBUSY;
 
+	/*
+	 * Powering the device IP down drops the link, and the host must
+	 * enumerate it again: take the pullup down and report a disconnect
+	 * now, as a VBUS drop would have, rather than resume as connected.
+	 */
+	if (mtu->connected) {
+		unsigned long flags;
+
+		spin_lock_irqsave(&mtu->lock, flags);
+		if (mtu->softconnect)
+			mtu3_dev_on_off(mtu, 0);
+		mtu->connected = 0;
+		mtu->bus_suspended = 0;
+		mtu3_gadget_disconnect(mtu);
+		mtu->g.speed = USB_SPEED_UNKNOWN;
+		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&mtu->lock, flags);
+		/* The reference the connection took in mtu3_link_isr(). */
+		pm_runtime_put(mtu->dev);
+	}
+
 	mtu3_dev_suspend(mtu);
 	synchronize_irq(mtu->irq);
 
@@ -1060,5 +1080,14 @@ int ssusb_gadget_resume(struct ssusb_mtk *ssusb, pm_message_t msg)
 
 	mtu3_dev_resume(mtu);
 
+	/* The pullup does not survive the power-down: assert it again. */
+	if (mtu->is_active && mtu->softconnect) {
+		unsigned long flags;
+
+		spin_lock_irqsave(&mtu->lock, flags);
+		mtu3_dev_on_off(mtu, 1);
+		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&mtu->lock, flags);
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 }
